  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880326",
      "title": "Lifecycle Hooks in the Composition API",
      "lectureOrder": 300,
      "videoOrder": 267,
      "sourceHash": "e10c54765e5c23dd882fb4afc3fd3042fe4d69a3960b1b9c87fe88a13d9152b3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "So that's how we can go from the options API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 6.92,
          "en": "to the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.92,
          "end": 10.89,
          "en": "Data is replaced with refs and reactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.89,
          "end": 14.08,
          "en": "methods are replaced with functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.08,
          "end": 15.57,
          "en": "which you expose to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 17.5,
          "en": "by returning them in that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.5,
          "end": 19.46,
          "en": "which you return in setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.46,
          "end": 22.87,
          "en": "Computed is replaced with the computed function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.87,
          "end": 26.99,
          "en": "and watchers are replaced with the watcher functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.99,
          "end": 28.81,
          "en": "Provide inject is replaced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.81,
          "end": 31.283,
          "en": "with the provide and inject functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 35.25,
          "en": "Now there's one more thing I wanna dive into",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.25,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "before we apply that all to a bigger project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 41.13,
          "en": "And that are lifecycle hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.13,
          "end": 44.79,
          "en": "There we have, for example, beforeCreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.79,
          "end": 47.56,
          "en": "and created in the options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.56,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "and we could simply add those methods to our config object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 54.653,
          "en": "How does this look like with the composition API?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 57.34,
          "en": "With the composition API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.34,
          "end": 59.99,
          "en": "we don't add those lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.99,
          "end": 62.86,
          "en": "to our component config object anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.86,
          "end": 66.94,
          "en": "instead we have functions which we can import from vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.94,
          "end": 69.84,
          "en": "which you can call inside of the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.84,
          "end": 72.5,
          "en": "But for beforeCreate and created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.5,
          "end": 74.45,
          "en": "there actually is no equivalent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.45,
          "end": 77.06,
          "en": "because these hooks are not needed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.06,
          "end": 81.08,
          "en": "because the setup method basically runs at the same time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.08,
          "end": 85.22,
          "en": "beforeCreate and created ran in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.22,
          "end": 87.34,
          "en": "So setup replaces these hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.34,
          "end": 90.87,
          "en": "Whatever you would have done in created or beforeCreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 93.563,
          "en": "should be done in the setup method itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.97,
          "end": 98.68,
          "en": "Now for beforeMount and mounted, it's different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.68,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "There we have the onBeforeMount and onMounted functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 105.85,
          "en": "which can be imported from vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.85,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "For beforeUpdate and updated it's similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 111.57,
          "en": "and the same for beforeUnmount and unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.57,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "Here we have onBeforeUnmount and onUnmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 116.93,
          "en": "So you see a pattern here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.93,
          "end": 119.08,
          "en": "Let's not also have a look at that in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.13,
          "end": 123,
          "en": "Back here, let's say in the user data component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123,
          "end": 126.95,
          "en": "as I mentioned, we're now not going to add created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.95,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "and mounted and so on here to our options object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 134.8,
          "en": "Instead, we're going to add them here in setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.8,
          "end": 137.53,
          "en": "by importing the required hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.53,
          "end": 138.6,
          "en": "Now as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.6,
          "end": 141.99,
          "en": "there is no onBeforeCreate and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 144.55,
          "en": "but there is a onBeforeMount,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.55,
          "end": 146.653,
          "en": "there is a onMounted, onBeforeUpdate, onUpdated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.487,
          "end": 155.403,
          "en": "and onBeforeUnmount as well as onUnmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 160.02,
          "en": "And I quickly restructure this to make it easier to read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.02,
          "end": 162.88,
          "en": "These are the lifecycle hook functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.88,
          "end": 164.723,
          "en": "which we can import from vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.09,
          "end": 168.54,
          "en": "Now how do we use them in setup?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.54,
          "end": 170.51,
          "en": "In setup, you simply call them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.51,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "like for example onBeforeMount, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.3,
          "en": "and you pass a function to them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.3,
          "end": 180.08,
          "en": "and this function will now be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.08,
          "end": 182.403,
          "en": "whenever this lifecycle hook is due.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.28,
          "end": 187.09,
          "en": "So here I can console log beforeMount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.28,
          "end": 191.483,
          "en": "or onBeforeMount, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 195.16,
          "en": "And we can now repeat this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.16,
          "end": 197.097,
          "en": "We also have onMounted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.22,
          "end": 201.547,
          "en": "so here I will print onMounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.28,
          "end": 205.503,
          "en": "We also have onBeforeUpdate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.98,
          "end": 211.143,
          "en": "so we print onBeforeUpdate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.02,
          "end": 216.41,
          "en": "We have onUpdated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.41,
          "end": 218.837,
          "en": "so here we can print onUpdated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.66,
          "end": 222.873,
          "en": "And we have onBeforeUnmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.28,
          "end": 227.543,
          "en": "and print onBeforeUnmount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.82999999999998,
          "end": 231.29,
          "en": "as well as here onUnmounted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.3,
          "end": 236.73,
          "en": "oops I mean here onUnmounted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.4,
          "end": 240.333,
          "en": "and print onUnmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 243.384,
          "end": 246.23,
          "en": "If we now saved it all and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246.23,
          "end": 249.83,
          "en": "we see onBeforeMount and onMounted here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.83,
          "end": 252.83,
          "en": "if I clear the console and click change age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.83,
          "end": 255.21,
          "en": "we also see onBeforeUpdate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.21,
          "end": 258.85,
          "en": "then our watcher runs and then onUpdated thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.85,
          "end": 261.4,
          "en": "once the update was applied to the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 261.4,
          "end": 263.26,
          "en": "and to the real DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.26,
          "end": 264.55,
          "en": "Well, and for unMounting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.55,
          "end": 266.87,
          "en": "we would need to get rid of user data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.87,
          "end": 270.02,
          "en": "which we can do with an if statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.02,
          "end": 271.74,
          "en": "for example, with v-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.74,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "If we now had some condition here that could get false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 278.15,
          "en": "this component would be removed from the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.15,
          "end": 279.82,
          "en": "and when that happens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.82,
          "end": 282.323,
          "en": "the onUnmount hooks would be called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.71,
          "end": 286.03,
          "en": "But I think the pattern should be clear here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.03,
          "end": 287.74,
          "en": "We see those logs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 287.74,
          "end": 291.62,
          "en": "and we see that this is how you can register code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.62,
          "end": 293.18,
          "en": "that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.18,
          "end": 297.21,
          "en": "at different phases of the lifecycle of a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.21,
          "end": 299.92,
          "en": "You simply call those special functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 299.92,
          "end": 301.77,
          "en": "which you import from vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.77,
          "end": 304.08,
          "en": "and you pass your function that holds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 307.55,
          "en": "your to be executed code to those functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.55,
          "end": 310.22,
          "en": "And that's how you work with lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.22,
          "end": 311.823,
          "en": "in the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
